<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREAN 3-YR YIELDS END FLAT ON BEARISH SENTIMENT.</title>
<headline>S.KOREAN 3-YR YIELDS END FLAT ON BEARISH SENTIMENT.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on benchmark three-year bonds ended Thursday's session flat as trading sentiment turned bearish under small new issues and tightened liquidity due to the central bank's deadline for won reserve requirements, traders said.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates close at 11.94 pct vs 11.94</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs close at 12.10 pct vs 12.05</p>
<p>* Average overnight call at 12.28 pct vs 11.99</p>
